export anchor TestOutput:
    description:
        Results go to stdout, one block per test, separated by blank lines, laid
        out at the terminal's width, no less than 40 columns and no more than
        100, or 100 when stdout isn't a terminal.

        ```text
        \\\
        ✗ FAIL   SaveButtonSaves                                  1:02
                 spec/tests/Editor.pi · editor, save
                 No handler saves the document
                 The Save button has no click handler. No function in src writes the document to disk.
        \\\
        ```

        The first line is the status as a mark and a word, ✓ pass, ✗ FAIL or !
        error, then the test's name, and how long it ran at the right edge, as
        minutes and seconds. The second, dimmed, is the file it is declared in
        and its tags. For a test against both with a result for each side, a
        line for the specification and one for the code follow, each with its
        own mark and word and its reason, so a test that holds in one and not
        the other shows both, though it fails.

        ```text
        \\\
        ✗ FAIL   SaveButtonSaves                                  1:02
                 spec/tests/Editor.pi · editor, save
                 spec ✓ pass  The spec says Save saves
                 code ✗ FAIL  No handler saves the document
                 The code has no save handler
                 The Save button has no click handler.
        \\\
        ```

        Then the agent's reason, aligned under the name, and for a failure its
        ASD-STE100 explanation beneath the reason, in the status's colour. The
        reason, the explanation and each side's reason are each printed as one
        line: not hard-wrapped, with no indent on continuation lines and no
        bar. The terminal wraps a long line, so a user can select a result in
        the console and copy and paste it as coherent text. A name too long for
        the line is cut with an ellipsis.
